# CarePlan Scheduler — Cline project rules

These rules apply to every task in this repository. Read them before every task.

## What this project is
CarePlan Scheduler is a standalone, multi-tenant scheduling app for Missouri home and
community-based services (HCBS).
- `packages/engine`: the rules engine (Phase 1, done). Pure TypeScript, no UI.
  Source of truth: `docs/ENGINE-SPEC.md`.
- `packages/import`: reads Fusion care plans (pasted text and PDF text). Pure TypeScript.
  Source of truth: `docs/IMPORT-SPEC.md`; fixtures in `docs/fixtures/fusion/`.
- `apps/web`: the React app (Phase 2): public site, accounts, Quick Schedule.
  Source of truth: `docs/APP-SPEC.md`. Visual target: `docs/design/quick-schedule-prototype.html`
  and `docs/design/tokens.css`.
If a prompt and a spec disagree, stop and ask.

## Hard rules (whole repo)
1. Build exactly what the current prompt asks. Do not start the next prompt, and do not
   refactor files the prompt did not name.
2. TypeScript `strict: true`. No `any`. No `// @ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error`. No default
   exports (except where a tool requires one: `vite.config.ts`, `playwright.config.ts`,
   `vitest.rules.config.ts`).
3. Complete every function and component you start. No `TODO`, no stubs, no placeholder
   returns, no "coming soon" screens, no lorem ipsum.
4. Never hardcode participant data, debug data or sample results in source. Test data lives
   only in test folders and uses identifiers like `P-TEST-01`, never real-looking names.
   The Quick Schedule example plan (APP-SPEC QS-12) is the one allowed built-in example.
5. Pinned versions only (below and APP-SPEC section 1). Install with exact versions
   (`--save-exact`). Never upgrade or add a package the prompt didn't name.
6. Before finishing any prompt, run every command in its "Finish" list. All must pass. Paste
   the summary lines into your final message.
7. Commit on the branch the prompt names with the commit message it gives. Never commit to
   `main` and never push with `--force`.

## Engine rules (`packages/engine`)
8. Every rule function is named after its spec ID (e.g. `ruleSCH08CalendarCheck`) and has
   JSDoc lines `@rule SCH-08` and `@source <source named in the spec>`.
9. Never recalculate and overwrite an imported Fusion authorization. Computed values are
   tagged `source: "derived"` with a `method`.
10. Never mark something compliant when its rule status is OPEN or PARTIAL: emit `REVIEW`.
11. Exact integer minute arithmetic. Round only where the spec names the function.
12. No I/O, no module-level mutable state in `src/`.

## Import rules (`packages/import`)
I-1. Same purity rules as the engine: no I/O in `src/`, no module-level mutable state, no
    logging. Never weaken a fixture's expected values to make a test pass.
I-2. Never commit a real care plan, participant name, DCN, address or PA number anywhere in
     the repo (code, tests, fixtures, docs, commit messages). Use the de-identified fixtures.
I-3. Participant name and DCN never go to storage, the URL, the console, error messages or
     Firestore (IMPORT-SPEC IMP-16).

## App rules (`apps/web`)
13. All schedule math comes from `@careplan/engine`. The app never re-implements units,
    rounding, composing or rule checks.
14. Colors, fonts, radii and shadows come only from `src/styles/tokens.css` through the
    Tailwind token names. No hex, rgb() or hsl() literals anywhere else (a test enforces it).
15. Every user-facing string follows APP-SPEC section 4.3: sentence case, plain words, buttons
    say what happens, errors say how to fix it. Use the exact copy the spec gives.
16. Accessibility is part of done: labels on every control, keyboard paths, visible focus,
    `aria-live` where the spec says, WCAG 2.2 AA (axe must report zero violations).
17. Public pages (`/`, `/quick`, `/rules`, `/privacy`) never import Firebase. Firebase code
    loads only through lazy routes. `scripts/check-bundle.mjs` must pass.
18. Never call `getAnalytics` or add any tracking, analytics or third-party script.
19. Quick Schedule state lives only in React state and `sessionStorage` key `cps.quick.v2`
    (without the participant's name and DCN). Never write it to Firestore, `localStorage`,
    the URL or the console.
19a. Every change a person makes to a schedule goes through the guard (APP-SPEC 5.7). Never
     add a path that changes the schedule without it.
20. Never edit `firestore.rules`, `docs/design/tokens.css`, `docs/APP-SPEC.md`,
    `docs/IMPORT-SPEC.md`, `docs/ENGINE-SPEC.md` or `docs/fixtures/` unless the prompt says to. If one seems wrong, stop and report.
21. Firebase calls live in `src/features/*/` service modules; components call those
    modules, never the Firebase SDK directly. Every Firestore error maps to copy from
    APP-SPEC 6.6.
22. No `console.log` in committed code. No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.

## Pinned versions (do not upgrade)
- Node 22 LTS. Package manager: npm workspaces. No pnpm, no yarn.
- Engine: typescript 5.9.3, vitest 3.2.4, luxon 3.5.0, @types/luxon 3.4.2, @types/node 22.20.5.
- Web: see APP-SPEC section 1 (react 19.3.1, react-router 7.18.4, vite 7.3.7,
  tailwindcss 4.3.3, firebase 12.19.0, and the rest of that table).
- Root dev: firebase-tools 14.27.0.
- pdfjs-dist 4.10.38 (web dependency; import dev dependency for PDF fixture tests).

## Style
- One concept per file, files under 300 lines.
- Engine: pure functions; dates as ISO strings `YYYY-MM-DD`, months `YYYY-MM`; local time
  `America/Chicago` converted with luxon only inside `src/calendar/time.ts`.
- App: function components and hooks; state with `useReducer` where several inputs interact;
  pure logic in `.ts` files next to the feature, tested without rendering.
